{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/229847-changeling-the-dreaming-more-than-one-musing-threshold","id":229847,"title":"Changeling the Dreaming - More than one Musing Threshold?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-15T19:25:27-07:00","id":229847,"title":"Changeling the Dreaming - More than one Musing Threshold?","content":"One of the easiest rules to ignore in Changeling is how you are only supposed to have one Musing Threshold. This is painfully annoying and hard to justify. But I seem to vaguely remember that there was a Merit that allowed you to have more than one Musing Threshold, but I can't find it. Can anyone help?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T19:59:03-07:00","id":229879,"title":"","content":"I always read the thresholds as more role playing guidelines than hard and fast rules, much like how a character's secondary legacy has no mechanical weight behind it. I'll double check with the book tomorrow to make sure. I don't have easy access to it right now though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T20:55:25-07:00","id":229909,"title":"","content":"Doesn't the Treshold just give you a bonus for one type of musing? Nothing more nothing less, it doesn't restrict you in any way but provides an incentive to use it instead of another type of musing. This is just out of memory though so perhaps it's best we wait for PookaKnight to check the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T21:00:44-07:00","id":230960,"title":"","content":"Here's what the book has to say on Musing Thresholds:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This specialty, called a Musing Threshold, usually reflects the changeling's own tastes, and the ways in which she is inspired in life. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A character who begins play without one can gain a specialty during play, and a character's specialty can change during the course of a chronicle. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At the beginning of a story, each player can establish a goal that he intends to fulfill with his Musing Threshold to earn Glamour. </div> </div> </div>There aren't really mechanics around the Musing Thresholds other than each character must have one. It reads more like something designed to give role playing ideas to the player instead of something that's supposed to limit them.<br /> <br /> As for the merit Mercurial is thinking of, I can't find anything along those lines in the core book or the player's guide. That doesn't mean something like that doesn't exist in a Kithbook, Fool's Luck, or one of the house books, but that's a lot of searching and not to mention feeling like a poor use of bonus points for something that's supposed to help spur player creativity as role playing guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T06:13:32-07:00","id":236399,"title":"","content":"Yes, again I completely agree with PookaKnight. I have never seen Musing (and Ravaging, from The Shadow Court) Thresholds as something that limits characters' actions. I have always used them just as a preference, not as a compulsion or a limitation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T10:59:22-07:00","id":239341,"title":"","content":"And actually, this is a very useful thing, this Musing Threshold since it allows characters to gain Glamour without going into a full Musing process with a Dreamer since these Musing Thresholds can be done with almost anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}